# scripts/opcount: `loosebench bench fenced N` reads a model's reply (a
# sentence and a markdown fence around a record's JSON) N times with
# json.DecodeLoose (wf10 JL); the cost of one read is the slope between the
# two sizes. The control is hand Go: the fence cut off by strings.Index and
# the body read by encoding/json into the record's struct. The floor finds
# the value's first and last brace and reads that by encoding/json: no
# scan of the text past what finding the value takes.
unit reply
sizes 20000 120000
args bench fenced {n}
control benchmarks/jsonloose/testdata/control
floor benchmarks/jsonloose/testdata/floor
